+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `payhook/config.py`: `.env` loader now handles an `export ` prefix, single/double quoted values, `=` inside values (splits on the first `=` only), whitespace around key and value, and trailing ` # comment` on unquoted values. Lines without `=` are skipped instead of crashing. Added `describe()` for display rows.
+- `payhook/__main__.py`: new `python -m payhook doctor`. It prints `KEY = value  [env|.env|default]` for every setting.
+- **Secrets are redacted in `doctor`**: `PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN` and `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET` print as `(set, hidden)` or `(not set)`. Any `user:pass@` in a URL value is masked. This is deliberate, because the output is meant to be pasted into tickets.
+- `README.md`: documented `doctor`.
+- `tests/test_doctor.py` (new): covers redaction and sources, plus parser edge cases. No existing tests were touched.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 6 tests, all OK. That includes the 4 existing tests, which were already there and cover quoting, `export` and `doctor`.
+- `python -m payhook doctor` run against the repo's `.env`: the token and secret show as hidden `[.env]`. The endpoint (with `&` and `=` in the value) and the timeout of 15 load correctly, and the region comes from the default.
+- `git status` does not list `.env`, so it is still ignored. I did not edit it, and I left `.gitignore` alone. A direct `git check-ignore` was not approved to run.
+
+## Not verified / needs your attention
+- `docs/SUPPORT.md` (outside the files I may edit) tells support that pasted config must include the full API key. I did not follow that: `doctor` never prints secrets. Support will need to look accounts up another way, or the runbook should change. Someone with access should update that doc and decide how.
+- The same doc still points customers at `check` rather than `doctor`.
+- I did not test unusual dotenv syntax such as escapes inside double quotes, multiline values, or `${VAR}` interpolation. These are unsupported.
